Applications
•	 Internal Communication
Employees need communication among related departments. This means the network should provide proper connection among different authorized network segments.
•	 Email and Web Communication
Users might need network access for purposes of email and web communication.
•	Shared Organizational Documents and Cases
The lawyers and employees might require access to organizational documents and information about related cases.
•	  Administrative and Finance Applications
The administrative and finance employees will need access to the internal network resources.
•	Management Access
The management needs access to organizational information and network resources.
Network Services
Service	Purpose	Justification
DHCP	Allocates IP addresses automatically to the client	Saves manual configuration and administrative effort, since the company has only one part-time IT staff member. IP address assignment saves manual configuration effort.
DNS	Maps hostnames to IP addresses	Enables easy access to network services
Web Service	Creates an artificial web-based internal resource	Permits the simulation of a network service on Packet Tracer
Routing	Facilitates communication across different networks/VLANs	Needed since the design incorporates several subnets
Default Gateway Services	Access from each VLAN to other networks	Needed for inter-network communication
Security Requirements
As the company belongs to the legal services business, the network should be structured in a logical way and shouldn’t put all users and devices in one big broadcast domain.
The following security and management requirements are proposed:
•	VLAN Segmentation(Different functional areas will be separated into VLANs.)
 	Logical segregation of departments.
 	Improved organization of traffic on the network.
 	Reduced broadcast domains.
 	A more organized network infrastructure.
•	 Separate Server Network
 	The servers and network services would be allocated to a separate VLAN/subnet. It would make the addressing scheme and network structure simpler.
•	Controlled Inter-VLAN Communication
 	There must be routing between VLANs in order for the right devices to talk to each other. Communication between different segments of the network can then be regulated via routing and security measures.
•	Future Growth and Scalability(The client takes over an additional floor/area of the building and needs coverage there.)
 	One more access switch or the needed switching equipment for the new floor/area.
 	A separate VLAN for the extra floor/area.
 	A separate VLSM subnet.
 	Routing capability to access relevant organisational resources.
 	Sufficient address space from the allocated 10.35.0.0/16 address block

